<!--
    PUF Invoice Example: Extensive Tax Invoice (Field Coverage Reference)

    Use Case: A reference that shows where the optional PINT AE business terms go in PUF.
              It combines three transaction types and the five VAT categories that can
              appear together on a tax invoice, which is broader than a typical invoice.
              Counterpart of the PINT AE examples "Standard invoice - Extensive" and
              "Standard tax invoice".

    Country: United Arab Emirates
    Format: PUF (Pagero Universal Format) 2.0
    Document Type: Tax Invoice (Type 380)
    Transaction Type: BTAE-02 = 10001010 (position 1 Free Trade Zone, position 5
                      Continuous Supply, position 7 E-Commerce)
    Target Format: Peppol PINT BIS Billing AE 1.0.4

    Scenario Description:
    Acme Trading LLC (Dubai) bills Burj Holdings PJSC (Abu Dhabi) for April 2026 under a
    12-month online supply agreement. The goods are delivered to a free zone end user in
    Jebel Ali. The five lines cover the VAT categories S, E, O, AE and Z. The invoice has
    line and document level allowances and charges, AED 5,000.00 charged to the buyer's
    card at checkout and a rounding amount. Total AED 23,723.50; AED 18,724.00 is payable
    and is charged to the same card on the due date.

    Key Fields (in document order):
    - IBT-168 Issue time; BT-22 note; BT-7 VAT point date, before the issue date
      (ibr-141-ae); BT-19 buyer accounting reference; BT-10 buyer reference
    - BG-14 Invoicing period; BT-13 / BT-14 purchase and sales order references; BG-3
      preceding invoice; BT-16 despatch advice; BT-15 receiving advice; BT-17 tender
      reference; BT-12 contract, with the contract value BTAE-05 in DocumentDescription;
      BG-24 supporting documents by URI and embedded; BT-11 project reference
    - BTAE-01 Free zone beneficiary in puf:RestrictedInformationParty (ibr-007-ae)
    - BT-28 / BT-45 trading names; BT-36 / BT-51 address line 2; BT-33 seller
      additional legal information; BG-6 / BG-9 contacts
    - BG-10 Payee, identified by its TIN (AE:TIN); BG-11 seller tax representative with
      its TRN (ibr-056)
    - BG-13 Delivery: date, GLN location, address (ibr-142-ae for e-commerce) and the
      delivery recipient's TRN as BTAE-23
    - BG-16 Payment instruction with payment card information (BG-18, at most one per
      invoice, ibr-066). PUF carries one payment means code per document, so send a
      single cac:PaymentMeans; the other UAE examples show a credit transfer (BG-17)
    - BG-20 / BG-21 document level allowance and charge; BG-27 / BG-28 line level ones
    - BT-113 paid amount and BT-114 rounding amount
    - Lines: BT-127 note, BT-133 accounting reference, BG-26 period, BT-132 order line
      reference, BT-156 / BT-155 / BT-157 item identifiers, BT-159 country of origin,
      BG-32 item attributes

    Not shown: BTAE-06 Frequency of billing. The PINT AE 1.0.4 syntax binds it to
    cac:InvoicePeriod/cbc:Description, while rules ibr-005-ae and ibr-160-ae validate
    cac:InvoicePeriod/cbc:DescriptionCode.

    Reference: UAE Electronic Invoicing Guidelines V2.0 (26 October 2026), 10.2.2;
               Peppol PINT BIS Billing AE 1.0.4
-->
<Invoice xmlns:cac="urn:pagero:CommonAggregateComponents:1.0" xmlns:cbc="urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:CommonBasicComponents-2" xmlns:puf="urn:pagero:ExtensionComponent:1.0" xmlns:ext="urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:CommonExtensionComponents-2" xmlns="urn:pagero:PageroUniversalFormat:Invoice:1.0">
